WEBVTT

00:00:29.446 --> 00:00:33.283
I was hoping the highway
would've gotten us off their turf.

00:00:33.283 --> 00:00:34.492
I'll accelerate.

00:00:34.492 --> 00:00:36.119
Do it!

00:00:39.789 --> 00:00:40.623
What?!

00:00:40.623 --> 00:00:42.751
What's that? What was that?

00:00:42.751 --> 00:00:44.419
Yo, Ramis.

00:00:44.419 --> 00:00:45.503
Zidd!

00:00:45.503 --> 00:00:50.091
Do you know inhuman beings?
Literally, non-human creatures.

00:00:50.342 --> 00:00:54.137
The boundary... Aurora Particles
leak from insulation space

00:00:54.137 --> 00:00:56.431
and cause a change in the natural laws

00:00:56.431 --> 00:00:58.683
and they become inhuman beings.

00:00:58.683 --> 00:01:02.395
Are you talking about that rumor
about the holes in our Aurora Field?

00:01:02.395 --> 00:01:04.022
Right.

00:01:04.022 --> 00:01:07.609
I've heard about that,
some kind of pollution, right?

00:01:07.609 --> 00:01:10.195
But I heard there's no harming people

00:01:10.195 --> 00:01:12.739
as long as you're away
from the field's boundaries.

00:01:12.739 --> 00:01:16.034
No harm? Well, I guess so.

00:01:19.037 --> 00:01:22.165
<i>Brave your truth and brave yourself</i>

00:01:22.165 --> 00:01:25.710
<i>So we can go somewhere with the dite</i>

00:01:25.710 --> 00:01:33.134
<i>Keep hope alive, now we</i>
<i>wanna find the new world</i>

00:01:35.637 --> 00:01:38.848
<i>Chizu o ushinatte samayotteiru machi</i>

00:01:38.848 --> 00:01:42.310
<i>Owariyuku sekai demo</i>

00:01:42.310 --> 00:01:49.025
<i>Karada no oku de hashiru</i>
<i>no o yamenai inochi o kikasete</i>

00:01:49.025 --> 00:01:52.320
<i>Tayasanai hikari o tozasanai hitomi ni</i>

00:01:52.320 --> 00:01:55.699
<i>Kawaitemo yakitsuketa</i>

00:01:55.699 --> 00:02:02.330
<i>Kizutsuku koto mo naku te ni</i>
<i>suru mono nante nanimo shinjinai</i>

00:02:02.330 --> 00:02:08.253
<i>Dareka ni mukatta hitosuji no omoi wa</i>

00:02:08.253 --> 00:02:16.094
<i>Yoake no you ni hagane no yami o kirisaku</i>

00:02:16.094 --> 00:02:20.432
<i>Itsuka brave your truth and brave yourself</i>

00:02:20.432 --> 00:02:24.102
<i>Dakara tsuyoku kaeru</i>

00:02:24.102 --> 00:02:30.066
<i>Kasaneta chikara mo inori mo</i>

00:02:30.066 --> 00:02:33.737
<i>Kousa suru mirai, kakaeta negai</i>

00:02:33.737 --> 00:02:37.157
<i>Dare no te ni mo watasenai</i>

00:02:37.157 --> 00:02:38.700
<i>Just tough and alive</i>

00:02:38.700 --> 00:02:43.705
<i>Kokoro o tsuraneru</i>

00:03:08.688 --> 00:03:10.690
What are you, an idiot?

00:03:10.690 --> 00:03:13.526
What kind of spider gets
tripped up by its own web?

00:03:13.526 --> 00:03:16.613
For someone below even a newborn baby spider,

00:03:16.613 --> 00:03:20.158
rushing past strand formation
and trying straight for web-making

00:03:20.158 --> 00:03:22.577
is biting off <i>way </i>more than you can chew!

00:03:23.578 --> 00:03:27.957
<i>Back then, I was simply</i>
<i>trying my hardest to get stronger.</i>

00:03:28.625 --> 00:03:33.797
<i>But then I came to Zuellni,</i>
<i>wanting to change that way of life.</i>

00:03:34.422 --> 00:03:37.050
Motion response at 1005. Here it comes!

00:03:52.774 --> 00:03:57.237
Layfon! What are you doing
spacing out in the middle of practice?

00:03:57.237 --> 00:03:58.863
<i>And yet</i>...

00:04:01.950 --> 00:04:05.453
"The Enemy That Lurks in Death's Ground"

00:04:05.954 --> 00:04:09.874
Tomorrow is the competition
between the 3rd and 11th Platoons.

00:04:09.874 --> 00:04:12.419
We'll take a break from training.

00:04:12.419 --> 00:04:17.799
You can go watch the competition
or get a little R&amp;R. I leave it to you.

00:04:17.799 --> 00:04:21.553
You don't gotta tell me twice. See ya!

00:04:21.886 --> 00:04:23.722
What will you do, Layfon?

00:04:23.722 --> 00:04:26.516
Watching other platoons compete
would be a learning experience.

00:04:26.516 --> 00:04:30.478
Uh, I... I already have plans.

00:04:30.478 --> 00:04:31.688
Oh.

00:04:31.688 --> 00:04:35.150
All right Nina, I'll see you there.

00:04:36.026 --> 00:04:37.652
Layfon.

00:04:37.819 --> 00:04:39.279
Yes, what is it?

00:04:39.279 --> 00:04:44.200
I don't know what you did in
the past to "fail" in the military arts.

00:04:44.200 --> 00:04:45.493
But...

00:04:46.036 --> 00:04:52.000
for the 17th Platoon to keep
winning, to become stronger...

00:04:52.000 --> 00:04:54.919
we're going to need your strength.

00:04:54.919 --> 00:04:56.880
Please, Layfon.

00:05:12.937 --> 00:05:15.398
<i>To become stronger...</i>

00:05:15.398 --> 00:05:16.066
Huh.

00:05:16.066 --> 00:05:19.903
For that to happen,
we're going to need your strength.

00:05:19.903 --> 00:05:22.030
Please, Fon-Fon.

00:05:22.030 --> 00:05:23.656
Senior Felli!

00:05:24.866 --> 00:05:26.368
Why did you suddenly--?

00:05:26.368 --> 00:05:27.911
I simply opened the eyes

00:05:27.911 --> 00:05:31.122
of a certain <i>someone</i>, so that
our leader's words do not make him

00:05:31.122 --> 00:05:33.667
act unwisely again.

00:05:33.667 --> 00:05:35.085
You heard?

00:05:35.085 --> 00:05:39.172
Think too much about someone
else and you'll make a fool of yourself.

00:05:39.172 --> 00:05:41.007
Th-That's just...

00:05:41.007 --> 00:05:43.968
Can you say it's not true?

00:05:43.968 --> 00:05:47.305
But if that's the case,
then the other day even you--

00:05:47.305 --> 00:05:48.348
What was that?

00:05:48.348 --> 00:05:50.684
Uh, nothing!

00:05:50.684 --> 00:05:53.144
That instance was a fluke.

00:05:53.144 --> 00:05:57.649
Furthermore, I am continuing
to explore what else I can do.

00:05:57.649 --> 00:06:00.235
I'm doing what I can, too!

00:06:00.235 --> 00:06:03.029
Like going out to eat with
Naruki and the others on my day off.

00:06:03.029 --> 00:06:04.406
That's rather small.

00:06:04.406 --> 00:06:06.324
You start small, and slowly but surely--

00:06:06.324 --> 00:06:08.159
It's <i>too </i>small.

00:06:17.544 --> 00:06:19.295
<i>Not yet?</i>

00:06:19.295 --> 00:06:22.966
Look, there are lots of things
I'm thinking about doing!

00:06:23.008 --> 00:06:25.176
But between training and cleaning
at the machinery department,

00:06:25.176 --> 00:06:26.678
I don't have any time!

00:06:26.678 --> 00:06:28.346
Now you're just making excuses.

00:06:28.346 --> 00:06:30.265
They're not excuses...

00:06:30.265 --> 00:06:32.600
That's enough. Don't follow me.

00:06:32.600 --> 00:06:35.895
We happen to take the same way home, that's all.

00:06:36.396 --> 00:06:38.982
Lay-ton...

00:06:38.982 --> 00:06:40.900
Oh no, he's gone.

00:06:40.900 --> 00:06:43.611
I wonder what relation the two of them have.

00:06:43.611 --> 00:06:45.405
Nakki! Mii-<i>chan</i>!

00:06:45.405 --> 00:06:47.907
Well, they're in the same platoon and all...

00:06:47.907 --> 00:06:51.411
They've already spent a lot
more time together than with us.

00:06:51.411 --> 00:06:57.375
If you don't watch out, Lay-ton
could be snatched up by his senior!

00:06:58.126 --> 00:06:59.544
Just kidding!

00:06:59.544 --> 00:07:03.923
We won't let that happen--we got your back!

00:07:03.923 --> 00:07:05.842
You're one to talk, given that <i>you're </i>stirring
things up.

00:07:05.842 --> 00:07:07.677
Anyway, it all comes down to tomorrow!

00:07:07.677 --> 00:07:09.804
Just stick to the plan. Okay?

00:07:09.804 --> 00:07:11.431
R-Right...

00:07:17.354 --> 00:07:20.899
Oh. So Naruki and Mifi can't make it.

00:07:20.899 --> 00:07:26.279
N-Nakki has to work security for the
competition.

00:07:26.279 --> 00:07:31.159
There was an opening...
And Mii-<i>chan </i>suddenly, um...

00:07:31.159 --> 00:07:33.995
has a story to, uh...

00:07:35.997 --> 00:07:40.210
The two of them sure are
working hard. But what should we do?

00:07:41.252 --> 00:07:45.465
Should we eat some other
time that's good for everyone?

00:07:47.967 --> 00:07:51.304
I, um... Uh...

00:07:51.304 --> 00:07:53.515
E-Either way!

00:07:56.643 --> 00:07:58.603
Sorry for the wait.

00:07:59.813 --> 00:08:02.315
Enjoy your meal.

00:08:02.315 --> 00:08:04.317
This looks delicious!

00:08:04.818 --> 00:08:08.697
They say there's usually a line for this place.

00:08:09.948 --> 00:08:15.412
Maybe it's empty today because
everyone's watching the competition.

00:08:15.412 --> 00:08:19.290
Meaning we get to eat
without having to wait. That's lucky!

00:08:19.290 --> 00:08:21.501
Yes, you're right.

00:08:23.670 --> 00:08:27.173
I wonder if May-cchi's
doing well right about now...

00:08:27.173 --> 00:08:30.385
"Ah, the beauty of female friendship"?

00:08:30.385 --> 00:08:32.012
I guess.

00:08:54.200 --> 00:08:56.411
<i>So he didn't come after all.</i>

00:08:59.581 --> 00:09:02.208
Um... Lay-ton?

00:09:03.251 --> 00:09:06.671
Are you concerned about the competition?

00:09:08.298 --> 00:09:10.508
No, not really.

00:09:13.553 --> 00:09:18.308
That was delicious! That shop
is also famous for its sweets,

00:09:18.308 --> 00:09:21.269
so I've been wanting to go at least once.

00:09:21.269 --> 00:09:26.107
Oh. I'm sorry. Maybe we
should have eaten dessert, too.

00:09:26.107 --> 00:09:28.526
It's okay! Anyway...

00:09:30.028 --> 00:09:31.654
Here.

00:09:32.697 --> 00:09:34.574
Did you bake these all yourself?

00:09:34.574 --> 00:09:41.915
Y-Yes. Um, if you like... Well...

00:09:41.915 --> 00:09:43.667
Uh, yeah.

00:09:43.667 --> 00:09:48.213
<i>Actually, I really don't like sweets.</i>

00:09:50.215 --> 00:09:52.550
Um, okay then.

00:09:56.888 --> 00:09:59.808
How are they?

00:09:59.808 --> 00:10:01.059
They're delicious!

00:10:01.059 --> 00:10:03.478
I'm so glad!

00:10:03.478 --> 00:10:06.064
I'd heard you wanted to work in a cake shop,

00:10:06.064 --> 00:10:08.566
but you can <i>already</i>
make such delicious cookies?

00:10:08.566 --> 00:10:10.402
Incredible!

00:10:13.279 --> 00:10:17.033
No, I think you're the incredible one, Lay-ton.

00:10:17.033 --> 00:10:23.248
At the competition,
you were so s-strong and cool...

00:10:23.248 --> 00:10:26.334
This is the only thing I'm any good at.

00:10:26.334 --> 00:10:28.211
That's not true.

00:10:28.211 --> 00:10:33.925
You have a goal and you're
already heading straight for it.

00:10:34.300 --> 00:10:37.137
I'm sort of envious.

00:10:38.930 --> 00:10:42.350
I wonder if I'll find one too.

00:10:42.350 --> 00:10:44.978
Right, Leerin?

00:10:48.690 --> 00:10:50.316
Mayshen!

00:10:54.070 --> 00:10:55.697
What's that?!

00:10:57.449 --> 00:10:59.534
Are you all right, Mayshen?

00:10:59.534 --> 00:11:01.161
What was that?

00:11:01.161 --> 00:11:03.997
It's... It can't be!

00:11:50.543 --> 00:11:53.129
The situation is extremely grave.

00:11:53.129 --> 00:11:57.217
Thirty percent of Zuellni's legs
have sunk into collapsed ground,

00:11:57.217 --> 00:11:59.386
making movement impossible.

00:11:59.386 --> 00:12:01.012
We can't get out?

00:12:01.012 --> 00:12:05.058
Normally, we could extract ourselves unaided.

00:12:05.058 --> 00:12:08.186
However... At the moment, we...

00:12:08.186 --> 00:12:11.564
We're overrun by larvals.

00:12:11.564 --> 00:12:12.899
Larvals?

00:12:12.899 --> 00:12:16.861
Oh no... Contaminoids?!

00:12:16.861 --> 00:12:20.115
Impossible! The city should
be moving to avoid the contaminoids!

00:12:20.115 --> 00:12:22.242
There's no way this should happen!

00:12:22.242 --> 00:12:26.079
The city can only avoid
that which is aboveground.

00:12:26.079 --> 00:12:28.289
This time, we think the
city stepped into the nest

00:12:28.289 --> 00:12:32.794
of a dormant mother that
had gone underground to lay eggs.

00:12:33.545 --> 00:12:36.715
Those newborn larvals are starving!

00:12:36.715 --> 00:12:42.679
Normally, the mother offers herself
up for food once she's done laying,

00:12:42.679 --> 00:12:47.017
but what happens when another
nutrient source is close at hand?!

00:12:47.017 --> 00:12:50.979
You know what this means, don't you?

00:12:51.855 --> 00:12:52.856
I've already advised

00:12:52.856 --> 00:12:55.358
--Please stick together while evacuating!
--that citizens evacuate the city.

00:12:55.358 --> 00:12:59.279
Military Arts students,
switch all dites to safeties off!

00:12:59.279 --> 00:13:00.572
Request that municipal police

00:13:00.572 --> 00:13:03.283
handle guiding and evacuating the civilians.

00:13:03.283 --> 00:13:07.579
Of course, you will form
the core of the contaminoid offensive

00:13:07.579 --> 00:13:09.622
and you must fight!

00:13:09.622 --> 00:13:11.499
Watch yourselves out there!

00:13:11.499 --> 00:13:13.251
Attack the contaminoids?

00:13:13.251 --> 00:13:16.046
Can we do it? <i>Us</i>?

00:13:16.046 --> 00:13:18.131
If you cannot, there is only death!

00:13:18.131 --> 00:13:22.510
However, we must survive at any cost!

00:13:22.510 --> 00:13:24.095
For the sake of those living in Zuellni...

00:13:24.095 --> 00:13:28.308
No, for our very futures!

00:13:37.233 --> 00:13:40.820
We will head to the northwest
sector along with 9th Platoon.

00:13:40.820 --> 00:13:43.365
Can't anyone get ahold of Felli?!

00:13:43.365 --> 00:13:44.240
Ma'am!

00:13:44.240 --> 00:13:45.367
Layfon!

00:13:45.367 --> 00:13:48.119
Maggot! What've you been
doing at a critical time like this?!

00:13:48.119 --> 00:13:51.790
Yes, the situation is bad!
We have to get out of here immediately!

00:13:51.790 --> 00:13:52.832
What are you saying?!

00:13:52.832 --> 00:13:55.710
Please hurry to the shelters.
We have to evacuate!

00:13:55.710 --> 00:13:59.506
Evacuate? Escape?! Don't be ridiculous!

00:13:59.506 --> 00:14:01.591
Those are contaminoids!

00:14:01.591 --> 00:14:04.594
Students with no battle experience
banding together and attacking...

00:14:04.594 --> 00:14:06.262
Won't have a prayer?!

00:14:06.262 --> 00:14:11.059
That's right! This isn't some
competition between students!

00:14:11.059 --> 00:14:12.852
You're going to your deaths!

00:14:12.852 --> 00:14:14.479
So what?!

00:14:14.938 --> 00:14:18.483
What's your point?
What else are our powers for?

00:14:18.483 --> 00:14:20.735
Why do they dwell inside us?

00:14:20.735 --> 00:14:24.030
To protect those who are
important to us. Isn't that right?!

00:14:24.030 --> 00:14:27.492
How could we be allowed to run away now?!

00:14:27.492 --> 00:14:31.454
It's too peaceful here.
You don't understand anything!

00:14:31.454 --> 00:14:35.458
Layfon... You're different from us. So why?

00:14:35.458 --> 00:14:39.629
With all the power you have,
why don't you get serious and fight?

00:14:39.629 --> 00:14:42.924
You don't know how terrifying
the contaminoids are!

00:14:42.924 --> 00:14:45.301
Or what it is to fight them!

00:14:45.301 --> 00:14:50.598
If we don't fight now, when will we?! Move!

00:14:50.598 --> 00:14:52.225
Ma'am!

00:15:15.081 --> 00:15:19.210
So these are contaminoids...

00:15:19.502 --> 00:15:22.130
Artillery unit, fire!

00:15:25.175 --> 00:15:29.929
Concentrate fire on the flying ones!
We can't let them get to the city!

00:15:29.929 --> 00:15:30.972
Roger that!

00:15:30.972 --> 00:15:35.643
I've got a date tomorrow.
There's no way I'm gonna die <i>here</i>!

00:15:40.482 --> 00:15:43.610
I won't be done in by things like those!

00:15:43.610 --> 00:15:45.236
Restoration!

00:15:47.280 --> 00:15:48.907
Charge!

00:15:58.458 --> 00:16:00.460
It's so hard!

00:16:18.812 --> 00:16:23.525
<i>There's no reason for me to fight.</i>

00:16:34.953 --> 00:16:36.579
I...

00:16:46.589 --> 00:16:48.591
Dammit!!

00:16:53.304 --> 00:16:55.724
Good! You're here!

00:16:56.182 --> 00:16:58.476
Layfon! What are you doing here?

00:16:58.476 --> 00:17:01.187
Can you make two settings for this dite?

00:17:01.187 --> 00:17:03.648
Huh? Two?

00:17:03.648 --> 00:17:05.275
Two!

00:17:08.153 --> 00:17:09.279
Ma'am!

00:17:09.279 --> 00:17:10.071
Fon-Fon.

00:17:10.071 --> 00:17:14.784
Ma'am... Felli, there's something
I want you to help me with!

00:17:16.578 --> 00:17:21.875
If larvals have appeared,
the mother is surely sleeping nearby.

00:17:21.875 --> 00:17:23.626
I need its precise location.

00:17:23.626 --> 00:17:25.378
Can you find it for me?

00:17:25.378 --> 00:17:30.467
This is a surprise.
Now even <i>you </i>tell me to use nen'i?

00:17:30.467 --> 00:17:32.510
But if you don't, everyone will die!

00:17:32.510 --> 00:17:37.223
We're the only ones who can do this. Please!

00:17:37.223 --> 00:17:41.853
Honestly. You're so hopelessly softhearted.

00:17:54.366 --> 00:17:55.325
There's no end to them!

00:17:55.325 --> 00:17:57.786
We can't do anything else. Fall back! Fall back!

00:17:57.786 --> 00:18:00.246
Wait! Don't leave your posts!

00:18:00.246 --> 00:18:03.500
If we don't stop them here, what will we do?!

00:18:04.250 --> 00:18:05.877
Shit!

00:18:10.048 --> 00:18:12.050
Nina! Look out!

00:18:26.106 --> 00:18:28.400
It's no good. I'll hit Nina.

00:18:29.359 --> 00:18:31.361
<i>I'm going to die.</i>

00:18:41.746 --> 00:18:43.623
Wh-What is this?

00:18:43.623 --> 00:18:46.251
You're all right, aren't you?

00:18:47.669 --> 00:18:49.087
Layfon!

00:18:49.087 --> 00:18:50.922
Don't tell me...

00:18:51.715 --> 00:18:54.843
I've found it. Direction: 1305.

00:18:54.843 --> 00:18:57.178
I will find a way in and guide you.

00:18:57.178 --> 00:18:58.346
Thank you!

00:18:58.346 --> 00:18:59.973
Nina!

00:19:00.807 --> 00:19:02.308
Layfon!

00:19:02.308 --> 00:19:04.310
You did this? Just what--

00:19:04.310 --> 00:19:07.605
There's no time to explain!
Please get out of here.

00:19:07.605 --> 00:19:08.106
But...

00:19:08.106 --> 00:19:11.860
Hurry! I can take care of any number of larvals,

00:19:11.860 --> 00:19:16.197
but if the mother calls for help,
it will be hard to do it alone!

00:19:23.413 --> 00:19:26.416
Any... number?

00:19:26.416 --> 00:19:28.043
Layfon...

00:19:29.127 --> 00:19:30.754
Well, well.

00:19:41.890 --> 00:19:44.976
Your time limit in the outside
world will be five minutes.

00:19:44.976 --> 00:19:47.854
Any more than that and
even your lungs will not last.

00:19:47.854 --> 00:19:49.481
I know.

00:19:53.693 --> 00:19:56.029
Please do not die.

00:20:27.352 --> 00:20:31.606
I came to Zuellni wanting
to stop fighting, and yet...

00:20:31.606 --> 00:20:33.608
Restoration-01!

00:20:39.155 --> 00:20:44.828
But now I fully understand.

00:20:44.828 --> 00:20:49.624
If I want to keep living,
this is the only thing I can do.

00:20:49.624 --> 00:20:51.042
This is...

00:20:51.459 --> 00:20:54.087
The world we live in!

00:21:08.727 --> 00:21:10.729
Is anyone injured?

00:21:12.188 --> 00:21:14.024
Are you all right?

00:21:14.024 --> 00:21:15.650
All right.

00:21:17.652 --> 00:21:19.654
Yes, this way!

00:21:27.620 --> 00:21:29.247
Layfon!

00:21:30.915 --> 00:21:32.542
Ma'am.

00:21:33.168 --> 00:21:34.753
I'm glad you're all right.

00:21:34.753 --> 00:21:37.547
You're an idiot.

00:21:37.547 --> 00:21:41.968
You went flying out of the city
without any external gear.

00:21:42.677 --> 00:21:45.680
That was a little too careless...

00:21:46.348 --> 00:21:47.974
Layfon!

00:21:48.808 --> 00:21:55.899
Sorry. I'm... a little tired. So I'll rest...

00:21:56.691 --> 00:21:59.944
Hey! Don't go to sleep out here like this! Hey!

00:21:59.944 --> 00:22:03.448
Hey! Layfon. Layfon!

00:22:03.823 --> 00:22:05.450
Lay...

00:22:08.036 --> 00:22:09.662
I swear.

00:22:10.705 --> 00:22:13.875
You did well.

00:22:35.313 --> 00:22:38.191
<i>Kioku no hate ni</i>

00:22:38.191 --> 00:22:46.741
<i>Sagashiteita risou no miraizu</i>

00:22:46.741 --> 00:22:57.794
<i>Nanika ga kowakute,</i>
<i>wakaranakute, hitori de furuete</i>

00:22:57.794 --> 00:23:09.222
<i>Anata ga miezu ni itsumo aisou waratte </i>

00:23:09.222 --> 00:23:18.148
<i>Kimi no ude no naka dakareteita</i>

00:23:18.148 --> 00:23:23.820
<i>Samete yuku yo ni koi o shite</i>

00:23:23.820 --> 00:23:29.367
<i>Yume no naka made tsurete itte</i>

00:23:29.367 --> 00:23:35.040
<i>Itsudatte kimi wa, itsudatte kimi wa</i>

00:23:35.040 --> 00:23:43.798
<i>Itsudatte boku ni yasashii uso tsuita</i>

00:23:54.017 --> 00:23:57.187
<i>Mayshen mistakenly receives</i>
<i>a letter addressed to Layfon.</i>

00:23:57.187 --> 00:24:00.106
<i>The girls are concerned with</i>
<i>the sender's relationship to Layfon</i>

00:24:00.106 --> 00:24:04.569
<i>but meanwhile, Layfon is invited</i>
<i>to Felli's house for some reason...</i>

00:24:04.569 --> 00:24:06.738
<i>Next time, "The Letter From Glendan," and...</i>

00:24:06.738 --> 00:24:08.128
<i>Restoration!</i>
